  "narrative": "The independent validation of the joint high-feature_038/high-feature_018 contrast resolves the central ambiguity introduced by H126. The originally registered positive feature_010 contrast is decisively rejected: discovery and validation both give opposite-signed raw contrasts of approximately -0.84 and -0.83 units, and the validation lower bound is -1.13 to -0.54. Thus, within the joint high-signature region, feature_010 positivity is associated with substantially lower outcome_001. I therefore keep H126 rejected and close it as a test of the positive direction, while closing the reversed claim H134 as accepted because its signed validation lower bound (0.539) is well above the 0.15-unit threshold. This establishes a dataset-specific non-monotone feature_010 pattern: positive contrasts overall and in many non-high or mid signature contexts, but a strong negative contrast when high feature_038 and high feature_018 co-occur. The accepted attenuation interactions for high feature_038 and high feature_018 are therefore not merely weak subgroup contrasts; the joint region can reverse direction. H26 is the main negative update: the discovery high-feature_038 feature_003 lowering estimate was supported weakly, but validation gives only 0.045 with an independent interval of -0.158 to 0.248, and even the lower validation bound is below the claimed meaningful threshold. I therefore leave H26 unresolved and deferred rather than treating high feature_038 as an independent context for feature_003 lowering. H87 is confirmed by independent validation and remains closed. H6 remains rejected after validation. The next most informative analyses should distinguish a genuine synergistic or threshold effect from additive attenuation: test the feature_010 interaction between high feature_018 and its complement within high feature_038, and symmetrically test the interaction between high feature_038 and its complement within high feature_018. I also propose robustness analyses of the joint lowering contrast after excluding feature_037-positive samples and after restricting to non-high feature_036, because feature_037 and feature_036 are prominent context variables and could affect compositional balance in this small joint cell. Finally, because validation weakened the high-feature_038 feature_003 signal, I registered an interaction test of whether feature_038 modifies the feature_003 contrast inside the non-high-feature_036 region, where the marginal feature_003 effect is otherwise rejected. All claims remain unadjusted associations within the supplied dataset, without causal or external-generalization interpretation.",
  "research_notes": "Validation synthesis update: H87 accepted/closed; H6 rejected/closed; H26 unresolved/deferred because validation failed to support high-f038 feature_003 lowering. H126 positive direction rejected/closed; H134 reversed joint-high feature_010 lowering accepted/closed and independently validated (discovery signed +0.848, validation +0.833, validation lower +0.539). Feature_010 map is now strongly context-dependent: positive overall and in many non-high or mid f038/f018 contexts, attenuated/reversed in joint high f038 and high f018. Do not call this causal or generalizable. Feature_037 lowering remains broadly validated. Feature_003 lowering remains anchored primarily to high f036; high f038 evidence is weak/unresolved. Next focus: distinguish synergistic joint-high reversal from additive attenuation via restricted interaction analyses (f018 among high f038; f038 among high f018), and test joint lowering robustness excluding f037 and outside high f036. Add feature_003 interaction f038 within non-high f036 to probe whether f038 has independent modifying role."
}

